31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems the current arrangement is stagnant and lacks transparency, which is exactly how resentment builds up.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found out that some people are actually okay with paying more if it means they get a spot they actually use!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The morning rush is a mess. People are shoving bikes aside just to get out, and the rain exposure is uneven.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Interesting. The ledger is practically empty of parking-related revenue. We've been ignoring the financial side of this entirely.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The administrative load is already significant. Adding a complex billing system will likely lead to another abandoned project.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, simplicity is key, but not at the cost of fairness. We cannot just let the same people keep the best spots forever.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that sounds so stressful! No one should have to move other people's bikes just to go to work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"It is a systemic failure. If the layout is ignored, the ""fairness"" of the allocation doesn't matter because the bikes get damaged.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, the ""administrative load"" is a convenient excuse for laziness. A simple fee structure would solve the funding issue.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"It is not laziness, Shunichi. It is a matter of sustainability. If the person in charge burns out, the system collapses.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We need a solution that balances the physical constraints Ryuji mentioned with a rotation that prevents the stagnation I found in the minutes.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,Maybe we can combine the ideas? A system that rewards those who use them daily but rotates the spots?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Rotation is only useful if we designate ""high-traffic"" and ""low-traffic"" zones. Otherwise, we just rotate the frustration.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Let's stop the dreaming. We need a system that is financially self-sustaining and doesn't rely on the treasurer's charity.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I suggest we prioritize a system that requires minimal monthly maintenance. A long-term fixed rotation is better than a monthly shuffle.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, a long-term fixed rotation still leaves people feeling cheated if they are stuck with a bad spot for a year.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I just want everyone to be happy! Let's find a way to make the ""bad"" spots better or the ""good"" spots shared.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The ""bad"" spots are the ones exposed to rain and blocked in. Any solution must address the physical layout first.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'm tired of the emotional pleas. Let's see the options and pick the one that actually makes sense on paper.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Agreed. Let us move to the options.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
