60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option B is too rigid and can lead to a year of misery for the unlucky. Option C is the most egalitarian and prevents ownership disputes.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option C sounds wonderful! No one has to fight over ""their"" spot, and everyone can just be friendly and share.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the only one that solves the shoving match. If we use double-tier racks, we maximize space and remove the ""territory"" mindset.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the only rational choice. It assigns a value to the resource and provides the building with a fund for maintenance.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option C is the most sustainable. It removes the need for a register, billing, and monthly reconciliation. It eliminates the administrative burden entirely.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, Option A creates a class system in the building. Those who can't or won't pay are pushed out, which creates the exact friction I fear.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shunichi, please! Let's not make it about money. Let's make it about helping each other. Option C is so much kinder.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, money doesn't fix the rain exposure or the morning congestion. It just puts a price tag on the frustration.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, a ""class system"" is just another word for ""market value."" If you want a prime spot, you pay for it. It's the most efficient way.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Efficiency is not just about money, Shunichi. It is about the time spent managing the system. Option A is a nightmare for the treasurer.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Option C removes the ""mine"" and ""yours"" mentality. It encourages people to be considerate of the space as a whole.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm so excited about Option C! It's like a community effort. Everyone wins!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. By removing the fixed spots, we remove the incentive to ""guard"" a space and the frustration of being blocked in by a specific neighbor.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,You are all choosing the path of least resistance. Option A is the only one that treats the parking as an asset rather than a charity.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I cannot support a system that will likely be abandoned in six months because the paperwork is too tedious. Option C is the only viable long-term solution.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,It seems we have a strong consensus. Option C protects the social fabric of the building while solving the physical congestion.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,Yay! I'm so glad we could agree on something that makes everyone feel included.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,It is the most logical choice given the physical constraints and the behavioral patterns I observed.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Fine. If you all prefer a chaotic free-for-all over a structured financial system, so be it. I'll vote for A, but don't come to me when the racks break.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The lack of management is the point. It is the only way to ensure the system doesn't collapse under its own weight.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
